## BOOT AND SSH ACCESS
1. Open Command Prompt
2. Ping trio
3. Enter password

## SYSTEM UPDATES
4. sudo apt update && sudo apt upgrade -y
5. sudo reboot

## BACK TO PI PROMPT
6. ssh pi@<hostname>
7. Enter password

## NETWORK CONFIGURATION FOR PORTABILITY
8. sudo nmcli dev wifi list
9. press q to get back to prompt
10. sudo nmcli connection add tyoe wifi ifname wlan0 con-name "NAME" ssid "WIFI-name"
11. sudo nmcli connection modify "NAME" wifi-sec.key-mgmt wpa-psk
12. sudo nmcli connection modify "NAME" wifi-sec.psk "WIFI_PASSWORD"
13. sudo nmcli connection modify "NAME" connection.autoconnect yes
14. nmcli connection show (if it shows green, it's connected. If white, it's idle)
15. Continue adding connection if needed

## PREPARE FOR NB-IOT (FUTURE PROOFING)
1. Enter in prompt:
  mkdir -p ~/network-configs
  cat > ~/network-configs/README.md << 'EOF'
  # Network Configuration Notes
  ## Current Networks
  - HOME_SSID: Primary development
  - LAB_SSID: University lab
  - FIELD_SSID: Field testing location
  ## NB-IoT Integration (Future)
  When NB-IoT module arrives:
  1. Module will likely appear as /dev/ttyUSB0 or similar
  2. Use NetworkManager's GSM/cellular connection type
  3. Command template:
     sudo nmcli connection add type gsm ifname "*" con-name "nbiot" apn "YOUR_APN"
  ## Fallback Priority
  1. Ethernet (if connected)
  2. WiFi (by priority)
  3. NB-IoT (lowest priority, for field deployment)
  EOF
